Z||000000||rx7speed||10-11-2001||04:11 AM||||just figured I would ask you guys<BR>the rx7 forum is down for some reason but anyway<BR>I just bought another rx7 and I think my 1/4 sux<BR>it has a header, presilencer (all 3 cats gone) intake filter, and removed choke<BR>here are the stats from my first 2 runs with the car<BR>rt    1.213    1.187<BR>60'   2.491    2.349<BR>330   6.822    6.691<BR>1/8   10.552   10.438<BR>mph   64.82    63.70<BR>1000  13.784   13.723<BR>1/4   16.451   16.416<BR>mph   84.53    85.23<P>first time I was running with 35psi on the rear tires and spun them through all of first. second run dropped the psi down to 23 and still spun them through first. though I was dumping the clutch at around 6000-6500 rpms(oops) no burn out before I launch though(still running street tires that are running thin now).<BR>I shift at around 7500 rpms though each run I missed the shift into third. when I hit the gate in third the shifter just stops and I hit the gas rev to 8- 8.5krpms and then have to let them drop before ti will go into gear.<P>any ideas to help me out. I am getting a new tranny soon since the one I have is shot as it is. also how much would it help if I was able to hit that gear first time round?<P>------------------<BR>who needs pistons I have rotary<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DreXteR||10-11-2001||09:23 AM||||Well, you should dump the clutch in mids revs like 4000 to make no or less spin tire. Second I think you have to work your reaction time. And third DONT TRY to run against 1st2m6 in his Lovely Fiero or he will strip all your fenders and doors.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>His 1/4 time is 12.9?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> <P>DreX<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/Fiero1.jpg">       <BR>  <BR>86 GT Turbo Intercooler Project - Total Restoration.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-11-2001||09:42 AM||||try launching at 42-4500.. the sudden jolt with the higher RPMs and not being in the real torque band just causes the wheel spin your having.. Burn out.. uum NO.. thats just a waste of time... any street tire thats not a DOT drag radial is a waste of your time and $ in a weak attempt to burn out/heat them up... they don't heat up like you think they do... i'm pullin 1.81 60' times and 8.1 in the 1/8th on my heavy 18s. a set of Yokohama A032s or the new Falken Azenis would help you hook up at the line and not drain your wallet like a DOT slick... they are just as sticky but 2/3rds the price. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsttree51.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||10-11-2001||09:42 AM||||My brother has an RX7 non turbo...he just puts that thing sideways everywhere he goes.  It is really fast, but hooking up is an issue...maybe some different tires.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-11-2001||09:43 AM||||LMAO!... great mind think alike... hunh Drex..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>---the carberated cars only make about 160hp at the wheels with LOTS of mods... (like the ones listed in his post) i see them on the dyno all the time... a 2nd gen turbo 2 with int/exh/no cats and boost controller will easily make 310 at the wheels... have you thought about additional fuel or different ignition? what flywheel are you using? <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
