Z||000011||1FST2M6||10-11-2001||03:19 PM||||aaagh.. it's a 2nd gen..  the 3 rotor motors are sweet.. but $1200 for a motor sound REALLY low.. does it include the ecu, exhaust and turbo nessasary to run the new engine? is it a street ported unit or stock?  yeah all fieros have independant rear suspension. I'd shy away from the BFGs just caseu thye are so pricey and the yoko or falken are just as sticky and will out last the bfg. an apex-i s-afc and 330cc injectors would help you quite a bit since you ditched your cats the added fuel will help i've got an air/fuel injector duty cycle monitor for sale  $120 (shipped-in the US) [not the one pictured - it's new in a box]<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmonitor.jpg">     <BR>for more go fast goodies for your car check out <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  tell em Travis sent ya... and give them a laundry list of what you'd like.. Ramona, Chad or Ed will set you up with decent pricing... the apex-i unit was still cheaper through excessive autosport though (in Sioux falls, SD) Gt Bastard has their link. <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
