Z||000013||rx7speed||10-12-2001||04:20 AM||||eh I want a fiero but it would not solve my problems<BR>so far the best car I had ( though only owned a 71 camaro that I miss still, but not over my rx7, and my 78 celica GT, still own and still ticking..... somehow)<P>the 20B (three rotor) is sweet but hella lot of money. I think at last count about 35k or so atleast on a third gen rx7. that includes labor and parts. <BR>the one I am talking about is a motor from a 2nd gen TII with a street port. the motor itself is about 850 including turbo. then the rest is on the ecu, wire harness, and a few other misc things plus shipping. <P>as for the BFG I donno. I do auto-x also sometimes and I heard a lot of good about them though if I can get a tire just as sticky and work for for drag and auto-x for less money then I am happy. thinking of the apex-i s-acf though would it help? thinking of  haltech maybe but heard a few  bad things about a stand alone ecu for a street car.<P>what is the stock inject for your car in cc? mine uses 440. thinking of getting some 550 prims and secondary. <BR>damn I want a A/F monitor also.<P><BR>you think I can gain much by a ported intake and throttle body?<P>and ****  you should see the size of the tubes comming off the block of my motor. <BR>there is only 2 exhaust pipes comming off the block they are about 2 1/4 inches. about as big as each tailpipe on my camaro<BR>sorry blabbing again<BR>damn I need some sleep<P>but thanx guys you are helpfull<P><P>------------------<BR>who needs pistons I have rotary<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||02:04 PM||||I'd like to take this opportunity to say how much I enjoyed reading this thread. It is an awsome change from what we normally see from the MR2 and 'Stang owners who pop up here from time to time- and just sit and piss & moan about how great their cars are and about how much Fieros suck.  This is really great!<P>Thanks to rx7speeed for being so cool- and you're welcome to hang out here whenever you want!  I hope we see more people like you around here. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||10-12-2001||02:51 PM||||Pick up a set of used R compound Autocross tires.<P>Easy to find , sometimes for free. Great for drag Racing on the cheap. Check your local club , usually you can pick up 2 tires for $50 and they will still have a good amount of rubber left on them , just not reccomended for rain. I picked up a set of 17" (4 tires) R comound Pirelli's for free from a local porsche racer who switched to 18's. They still have lots of tread left.<P>Also with the stiff construction of an R compound or autocross tire you will find you can run them really low..espcally on a light car such as an Rx7. I can run my rears down to about 18psi before you can notice the tire is low (still sidewall).<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000016||rx7speed||10-13-2001||02:10 AM||||how could I say your fieros suck?<BR>I admit I would not take one over my rx7 but I would be far from saying they suck. how many friggen mid engine cars do you see driving around that can pull some sweet runs on the strip then move over to the twisties.<BR>oh yeah not to mention you can fit a v8 in those things :-) <BR>right now I am debating on what car I want to pick up and it is between an MR2 turbo and a fiero. love the mid engine design<BR>need something to drive around while I am converting mine to a turbo<P>but yeah I think all cars are cool<BR>sorry just going off<P>||||reg||1
